                                "sense_id": "1efc17c0-f00c-38ed-b8b2-0a70a4a22edc",
                                "text": "The Roman historian Tacitus does not simply tell what has happened in a past long past so that it will be preserved for the present and into an endless future; rather, he pretells what has happened, in effect transposing history (necessarily of the past) into prediction (necessarily of the future)."
